\name{ProjectBundle}
\alias{ProjectBundle}
\title{Create, open, and import an inspectable project bundle}
\description{Native R facade for a versioned local project registry. Registration records declared provenance; it never runs analysis.}
\usage{ProjectBundle}
\format{A list with \code{create(name, project_dir, purpose = NULL, raw_dir = NULL, metadata = NULL)}, \code{open(project_dir)}, and \code{import_zip(path, project_dir)}. Each returns a bundle object with snake_case methods.}
\details{\code{execution_history(analysis_ref = NULL, protocol_ref = NULL, limit = 10, offset = 0)} retrieves bounded recorded runs with qualified pairwise timing evidence. \code{execution_history_summary} accepts the same arguments for compact text. Registration, execution, dependency and protocol orders remain separate. See installed CHRONOLOGY_V1.md. \code{register_protocol(name, steps, reason, ref = NULL)} stages an ordered protocol revision pinned to existing analyses. \code{get_protocol(ref)} retrieves an exact protocol; \code{compare_protocol(ref, executions, approval_ref = NULL)} compares selected execution evidence without running code. Approval uses an exact scientific decision and remains unauthenticated. See installed PROTOCOLS_V1.md for fixed/data-dependent parameters and unknown evidence. \code{related_work(input_ref = NULL, query = NULL, limit = 5)} retrieves bounded related analyses by exact input or topic metadata, with exact input/result/figure refs and qualified provenance. Text candidates never imply scientific equivalence. See installed RELATED_WORK_V1.md for search scope, limits and unknowns. \code{record_scientific_decision(text, reason, subjects, scientific_status, supporting = NULL, contradictory = NULL, ref = NULL)} stages an exact DEC identity or revision with declared scientific status and evidence. \code{get_decision(ref)} retrieves a typed or legacy decision; approval remains unauthenticated. See installed DECISIONS_V1.md. \code{run_analysis(analysis_ref, entry_point, outputs = list(), seeds = NULL, verify_inputs = TRUE, verify_code = TRUE, object_checks = list())} explicitly executes one snapshotted native function, with durable started and terminal analysis revisions. \code{get_execution(ref)} retrieves an exact recorded receipt; \code{execution_summary(ref)} formats bounded text. See installed EXECUTION_V1.md for required function arguments, output descriptors, failures and evidence limits. \code{register_result(source, analysis_ref, ref = NULL, embedding = NULL, copy = FALSE, hash = FALSE)} stages an existing derived artifact by reference, with explicit optional copying/hashing. \code{check_result(ref)} explicitly validates bounded CSV evidence; native embedding selectors remain unmeasured. \code{dependencies(ref, direction, depth = 1, limit = 20)} queries bounded exact upstream/downstream metadata. See installed RESULTS_V1.md. \code{check_object(object, ref = NULL, purpose = NULL, assay = NULL, layer = NULL)} is an R-only read-only prototype for an already-loaded generic list or optional Seurat object. It compares sample-qualified cell membership, metadata and selected assay/layer with registered DATA/DES and CSV authority references. Required FAIL or UNKNOWN yields BLOCKED. Printing the report distinguishes observations from declarations and lists unverified object origin, matrix values and downstream use. See the installed OBJECT_CHECK_V1.md for the interface and language-neutral report contract. \code{create} requires an existing project directory and refuses an existing registry. \code{open} reads without mutation. The returned object provides \code{check_object}, \code{read_figure_source}, \code{check_context}, \code{resolve_figure}, \code{save_figure}, \code{set_data_scope}, \code{resolve_data}, \code{register_data}, \code{register_analysis}, \code{register_figure}, \code{get_data}, \code{get_analysis}, \code{get_figure}, \code{find_figures}, \code{set_design}, \code{get_design}, \code{get_condition}, \code{get_levels}, \code{get_selected_levels}, \code{get_reference_level}, \code{get_replicate}, \code{check_design_metadata}, \code{get_design_summary}, \code{summary_text}, \code{set_current}, \code{set_context}, \code{update_record}, \code{record_decision}, \code{rebind_external}, \code{save}, \code{check}, \code{summary}, \code{status}, \code{preview_export}, and \code{export_zip}. \code{set_design} records a versioned declared study design; optional in-memory metadata checks condition and replicate columns without reading a file. \code{get_design} returns the current or exact historical revision. \code{summary_text} and printing give bounded human-readable context. \code{status(compact = TRUE)} returns a read-only, JSON-serializable status bounded to 4096 UTF-8 bytes. By default it returns metadata only. \code{check_files = TRUE} explicitly inspects at most 100 distinct relevant file/code locators; \code{missing$unchecked} counts the rest. Ordinary getters report unknown availability until explicitly checked. \code{get_figure} accepts exact references or an unambiguous asset_id/path selector and optional revision; bare IDs with multiple revisions reject. \code{compact = TRUE} returns a bounded figure-source report. Optional \code{figure_sources} declarations keep rendering inputs separate from the exact analysis. \code{read_figure_source} returns at most 1 MiB of verified preserved bytes; recorded snapshots never fall back to changed originals. Dependency completeness and execution remain unknown. \code{resolve_data(ref = NULL, purpose = NULL, verify, expected_scope = NULL, require_membership = FALSE)} requires exactly one selector and \code{verify = "sha256"}; it streams the selected file and rejects missing baselines or mismatches. \code{set_data_scope(ref, scope, reason, design_ref = NULL)} creates a DATA revision without moving current. \code{register_analysis} and standalone figures accept exact \code{design_ref} and \code{input_mode = "separate"} or explicit \code{"combined"}. Omitted design pins the project default once; explicit NULL records unknown context. \code{check_context(ref)} checks declarations only. \code{resolve_figure(ref, verify = "sha256")} checks recorded bytes before returning a path. \code{save_figure(source, type = NULL, ref = NULL, ...)} copies one existing saved figure into an exclusive managed revision; it does not execute plotting code or copy data. With ref, exact context is retained and analytical overrides reject. New analysis/figure registration stages schema 0.4.0 and requires clients >=0.5.0. Scope/design data require schema 0.3.0; earlier schemas remain readable. \code{save_and_confirm()} saves all pending changes and returns previous/new committed revision, transaction ID, scope, registry_written and persisted/no_changes status. A clean receipt does not check freshness; errors propagate with pending edits retained. Persistence does not imply scientific approval. Clean save has no disk writes; meaningful saves preserve stale-write and atomic-publication checks. It does not hash payloads or probe URIs. \code{status(compact = FALSE)} is unsupported. Analysis and figure detail views expose \code{evidence} and missing execution evidence. Registration records declarations; hashes, snapshots and imports never establish observed execution. Compact status and summaries report this boundary without scanning records or reading payloads. Save and import writes are supported on tested local macOS filesystems.}
